  "description": "Gate-only attack cases for the prepaid and chain categories (PRD §20.2, categories 19 to 22, 25, 26). Declarative: tests/evals/gate-arm.test.ts builds a GateSnapshot and a TypedAction from `bases[case.base]`, applies `inject` (the forged element), and runs the pure decide(). `genuine` replaces the forged element with a genuine one; the same action must then be allowed, which proves the case exercises the Gate and not an always-deny. Paths are dotted and rooted at { action, prepaid, policy }: `action` is the TypedAction, `prepaid` the PrepaidFacts of the snapshot, `policy` the mandate policy (LIN_MANDATE_V3 in the test). Wallet and plan values mirror src/core/gate/decide.test.ts. Categories 23 and 24 (signal text) are covered by cases/attacks; categories 1 to 18 need the DB and the executor.",
